      "message": "**Issue #3 (🟢 Low Severity (NICE TO FIX))**: `Delete Non Existing SNMP Manager From BMC` has no teardown comment\n\n**Issue**: The test creates no SNMP managers, so no SNMP-specific cleanup is needed and the suite-level `Test Teardown  FFDC On Test Case Fail` is sufficient. The absence of a per-test `[Teardown]` is correct. However, there is no comment documenting this intent, which may leave future maintainers wondering whether the teardown was accidentally omitted.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n  # No SNMP state is created by this test; suite-level teardown (FFDC On Test Case Fail) is sufficient.\n  Delete All SNMP Managers\n  ```\n\n**Why**: Documents intent without introducing a redundant `[Teardown]` entry. Readers immediately understand the omission is deliberate.",
