      "message": "**Issue #2 (🟡 Medium Severity (SHOULD FIX))**: Hard-coded `Sleep 5s` with no justification comment\n\n**Issue**: The 5-second sleep precedes the `Read` call and is the sole mechanism for waiting for trap output. Other negative tests in this suite that test missing trap dispatches do not rely on a hard-coded sleep — they either do not start the listener at all or use the existing `delay` mechanism. The sleep value is undocumented (no inline comment explains why 5 s is sufficient/safe), making it fragile: too short on slow environments, too long in CI.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n  Sleep  5s  # Allow time for any spurious SNMP trap to arrive before asserting absence.\n  ```\n\n**Why**: Undocumented sleeps are a maintenance risk and a common source of flaky tests. Adding the comment is the minimal fix; replacing with `Read  delay\u003d5s` is the preferred solution.",
